WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:03.591
Ambassador at large for global

00:00:03.858 --> 00:00:04.892
criminal justice.

00:00:04.959 --> 00:00:06.227
She's joining me now from her

00:00:06.494 --> 00:00:06.994
trip to Bangladesh.

00:00:08.896 --> 00:00:09.396
Ambassador Van Schaack, welcome

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:10.063
to the program.

00:00:10.097 --> 00:00:13.667
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.370
&gt;&gt; Can I ask you to start with

00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:17.738
Syria?
We are getting more and more

00:00:18.005 --> 00:00:22.443
complaints that actual illegal

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.911
none intervention is hopping.

00:00:24.912 --> 00:00:25.746
That bashar al-assad is not

00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:27.448
allowing humanitarian access

00:00:27.715 --> 00:00:28.249
despite international law.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.821
&gt;&gt; Indeed, the arbitrary

00:00:34.088 --> 00:00:35.056
withholding of unitarian aid in

00:00:35.322 --> 00:00:36.924
an armed conflict situation can

00:00:37.191 --> 00:00:37.958
be a violation of the laws of

00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:38.725
war.

00:00:38.926 --> 00:00:40.127
And using starvation as a

00:00:40.394 --> 00:00:42.930
weapon of war is a criminal

00:00:43.164 --> 00:00:43.998
punishable war crime.

00:00:44.265 --> 00:00:45.099
Here we have a situation where

00:00:45.366 --> 00:00:47.902
it seems as if president Assad

00:00:48.169 --> 00:00:49.970
is really limiting the ability

00:00:50.237 --> 00:00:53.007
for humanitarian aid in this is

00:00:53.274 --> 00:00:53.841
a region that is largely

00:00:54.108 --> 00:00:55.142
controlled by rebel groups and

00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:56.944
opposition groups, which

00:00:57.111 --> 00:00:58.012
suggest that this is by design.

00:00:58.279 --> 00:00:59.213
&gt;&gt; And he has complained and

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.015
his government has complained

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:02.083
that it's all about sanctions

00:01:02.349 --> 00:01:03.818
imposed by the international

00:01:04.085 --> 00:01:04.518
community.

00:01:04.518 --> 00:01:05.853
But we have been told by U.S.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.121
Government John Kirby just on

00:01:07.388 --> 00:01:09.990
Friday that there are

00:01:10.257 --> 00:01:11.792
exemptions, and that sanctions

00:01:12.059 --> 00:01:14.962
do not limit humanitarian aid,

00:01:15.162 --> 00:01:15.863
especially in the

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:16.630
circumstances.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:18.199
Is that correct ambassador?

00:01:18.966 --> 00:01:19.466
&gt;&gt; Indeed.

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:22.970
Sanctions regimes have waivers

00:01:23.237 --> 00:01:24.171
within them for the provision

00:01:24.438 --> 00:01:24.972
of humanitarian aid.

00:01:25.172 --> 00:01:27.007
This would include food,

00:01:27.274 --> 00:01:29.944
medical care, as well as in a

00:01:30.211 --> 00:01:31.245
crisis situation like we have

00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:32.046
here.

00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:36.050
But the problem is that with

00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:37.952
the period in the security

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:38.986
council, there were three

00:01:39.253 --> 00:01:41.889
pathways to provide a to Syria

00:01:42.156 --> 00:01:42.656
during the conflict.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.992
Russia vetoed those

00:01:45.092 --> 00:01:45.559
resolutions.

00:01:45.559 --> 00:01:46.293
Now there's only one route to

00:01:46.994 --> 00:01:47.928
provide humanitarian aid.

00:01:48.195 --> 00:01:48.996
That route has not been damaged

00:01:49.263 --> 00:01:50.030
by the earthquake.

00:01:50.998 --> 00:01:51.999
And so in order to force the

00:01:52.266 --> 00:01:54.001
provision of military aid, we

00:01:54.268 --> 00:01:55.002
would need a new security

00:01:55.136 --> 00:01:59.140
council resolution, to create a

00:01:59.406 --> 00:01:59.906
new pathway.

00:02:00.174 --> 00:02:01.008
The fears that Russia will veto

00:02:01.008 --> 00:02:04.044
that again in support of its

00:02:04.311 --> 00:02:04.811
client state Syria.

00:02:05.179 --> 00:02:07.047
&gt;&gt; So ambassador, this leads me

00:02:07.314 --> 00:02:09.283
into the important, the equally

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.018
important conversation about

00:02:11.285 --> 00:02:12.153
holding Russia accountable for

00:02:12.419 --> 00:02:13.320
crimes inside Ukraine.

00:02:13.988 --> 00:02:16.056
But if you can't even get

00:02:16.323 --> 00:02:18.025
Russia, it is diplomatic

00:02:18.292 --> 00:02:20.027
capacity, to allow a

00:02:20.294 --> 00:02:22.062
humanitarian aid into Syria,

00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:24.098
what help do you have of

00:02:24.365 --> 00:02:26.000
holding them accountable for

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:29.770
the direct accusation of war

00:02:30.037 --> 00:02:30.671
crimes and crimes against

00:02:31.038 --> 00:02:31.372
humanity?

00:02:31.372 --> 00:02:37.611
&gt;&gt; Indeed, there are three

00:02:37.878 --> 00:02:39.246
pathways adjust as that

00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:39.980
operational.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:40.480
The right of the courts and

00:02:40.714 --> 00:02:41.115
Ukraine.

00:02:41.115 --> 00:02:41.615
And as you mention, there's

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:43.551
more than 65,000 incidents of

00:02:43.817 --> 00:02:45.219
war crimes and other potential

00:02:45.486 --> 00:02:46.287
atrocities that have been

00:02:46.554 --> 00:02:47.054
registered.

00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:49.323
The course their operational,

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.491
there are war crimes teams.

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:52.593
International community,

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:53.560
including tonight, states have

00:02:53.727 --> 00:02:54.228
been funding the provision of

00:02:54.495 --> 00:02:56.197
experts who have come from the

00:02:56.463 --> 00:02:58.199
worlds war crime tribunals to

00:02:58.465 --> 00:02:59.400
assist the prosecutor general

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.669
and this incredible challenge.

00:03:01.936 --> 00:03:03.204
Pathway them or two is the

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.471
international criminal court,

00:03:04.738 --> 00:03:06.307
also currently seized of the

00:03:06.574 --> 00:03:09.143
situation, because Ukraine has

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.178
consented to the exercise of

00:03:11.445 --> 00:03:11.945
jurisdiction.

00:03:11.946 --> 00:03:12.446
And finally of European courts

00:03:12.713 --> 00:03:14.348
and legal authorities that are

00:03:14.615 --> 00:03:16.350
starting investigations working

00:03:16.617 --> 00:03:17.451
through a joint investigation

00:03:17.718 --> 00:03:20.154
team, sharing information, and

00:03:20.421 --> 00:03:21.322
strategies in order to be able

00:03:21.589 --> 00:03:22.323
to bring --

00:03:23.224 --> 00:03:24.358
one perpetrators come within a

00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:25.125
jurisdiction.

00:03:25.192 --> 00:03:27.294
This however is the major

00:03:27.561 --> 00:03:27.995
challenge.

00:03:27.995 --> 00:03:29.196
As perpetrators remain in

00:03:29.463 --> 00:03:30.364
Russia, it will be very

00:03:30.631 --> 00:03:31.532
difficult for many of these

00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:34.301
justice pathways to operate

00:03:34.568 --> 00:03:35.269
unless in absentia trials are

00:03:35.536 --> 00:03:36.036
allowed.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.238
But none of these efforts

00:03:37.504 --> 00:03:39.206
require the consent of Russia,

00:03:39.473 --> 00:03:40.274
and so all of these

00:03:40.541 --> 00:03:41.242
investigations are moving

00:03:41.508 --> 00:03:41.909
forward.

00:03:41.909 --> 00:03:43.277
&gt;&gt; So just quickly, will trials

00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:44.445
in absentia be allowed?

00:03:47.147 --> 00:03:47.648
Is there precedence for that?

00:03:47.915 --> 00:03:49.483
&gt;&gt; There is precedent, and one

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.551
of the Ukrainian system, they

00:03:51.118 --> 00:03:52.286
are allowed, and there have

00:03:52.553 --> 00:03:53.287
been some cases.

00:03:53.554 --> 00:03:55.189
For example, some cases of

00:03:55.456 --> 00:03:56.290
sexual violence and other war

00:03:56.557 --> 00:03:57.424
crimes have been brought in

00:03:57.691 --> 00:03:59.226
absentia where a defendant was

00:03:59.493 --> 00:04:00.461
identified, but they did not

00:04:00.728 --> 00:04:01.662
have him in custody.

00:04:04.365 --> 00:04:05.132
International criminal court

00:04:05.132 --> 00:04:06.233
however cannot exercise

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.134
jurisdiction in absentia.

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:08.369
All it can do is issue an

00:04:08.636 --> 00:04:10.137
arrest warrant, and then

00:04:10.404 --> 00:04:11.372
ultimately confirm charges

00:04:11.639 --> 00:04:12.406
against individual.

00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:13.407
But it cannot move forward

00:04:13.674 --> 00:04:14.608
without the custody of the

00:04:15.142 --> 00:04:17.278
accused.
&gt;&gt; Can I ask you about the

00:04:17.544 --> 00:04:18.312
various pathways, as you

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:21.248
mentioned, they just seem to be,

00:04:21.515 --> 00:04:22.416
I'm not quite as a hodgepodge,

00:04:22.683 --> 00:04:24.184
but an alphabet soup of

00:04:24.451 --> 00:04:25.519
different jurisdictions from

00:04:25.786 --> 00:04:28.155
the Ukraine to the

00:04:28.422 --> 00:04:29.290
international criminal court,

00:04:29.556 --> 00:04:30.357
to Europe, et cetera.

00:04:32.192 --> 00:04:34.194
How does that help or

00:04:34.461 --> 00:04:36.263
complicate the efforts to

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:37.164
streamline the pursuit of

00:04:37.231 --> 00:04:37.731
justice?

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:41.835
&gt;&gt; And the, you often get asked

00:04:42.102 --> 00:04:43.504
if this is a chaotic situation.

00:04:43.771 --> 00:04:45.372
But what I preferred is

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:46.139
decentralized.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:46.774
There are a number of different

00:04:47.174 --> 00:04:49.343
nodes where justice is

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:50.044
happening.

00:04:50.044 --> 00:04:50.544
But European authorities are

00:04:50.778 --> 00:04:51.612
increasingly united and

00:04:51.879 --> 00:04:53.347
coordinated amongst themselves

00:04:53.614 --> 00:04:56.517
under the umbrella of the euro

00:04:56.784 --> 00:04:57.518
just genocide network, but also

00:04:57.785 --> 00:04:58.686
this joint investigative team

00:04:59.186 --> 00:05:00.387
that many European states have

00:05:00.654 --> 00:05:01.488
joined, that includes the

00:05:01.755 --> 00:05:02.656
prosecutor of the international

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:03.690
criminal court.

00:05:03.757 --> 00:05:04.658
And so while there are a number

00:05:05.426 --> 00:05:06.360
of efforts happening around the

00:05:06.627 --> 00:05:07.594
world, they are increasingly

00:05:07.861 --> 00:05:09.563
coordinated and talking amongst

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.598
themselves, sharing information,

00:05:11.865 --> 00:05:14.535
sharing potential evidence, all

00:05:14.802 --> 00:05:15.302
in the insist of justice.

00:05:15.502 --> 00:05:16.503
&gt;&gt; What should people in

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:18.505
Ukraine expect.

00:05:18.772 --> 00:05:20.507
What are the realistic

00:05:20.774 --> 00:05:21.408
expectations.

00:05:21.675 --> 00:05:22.509
We've talked about tens of

00:05:22.776 --> 00:05:24.445
thousands of allegations, of

00:05:24.712 --> 00:05:26.480
crimes, we talked about all of

00:05:26.747 --> 00:05:27.381
the groups that have been

00:05:27.648 --> 00:05:29.383
funded and really seem to want

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:30.718
to, including Ukrainian human

00:05:31.218 --> 00:05:32.586
rights and other groups inside

00:05:32.853 --> 00:05:33.654
the country there.

00:05:34.355 --> 00:05:37.358
And yet, we know, I guess, from

00:05:37.624 --> 00:05:39.593
president, that these processes

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.627
take a very long time.

00:05:42.429 --> 00:05:43.664
What should people who have

00:05:43.931 --> 00:05:45.566
lost their family members or

00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:47.434
who have been violently

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:49.370
attacked, sexually attacks,

00:05:49.636 --> 00:05:50.371
what should they expect

00:05:50.637 --> 00:05:53.440
realistically?

00:05:53.707 --> 00:05:54.608
&gt;&gt; They should expect that the

00:05:54.875 --> 00:05:55.375
international community

00:05:55.609 --> 00:05:56.510
delivers justice wherever it

00:05:56.777 --> 00:05:57.478
can be found.

00:05:58.345 --> 00:05:59.513
This will involve cases in

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.348
Ukrainian courts, and the

00:06:01.615 --> 00:06:02.449
prosecutor general will have

00:06:02.716 --> 00:06:04.451
the unenviable task of sifting

00:06:04.718 --> 00:06:08.689
through those 65 incidents and

00:06:09.256 --> 00:06:09.756
determining which one there is

00:06:09.857 --> 00:06:11.358
significant evidence to prove,

00:06:11.625 --> 00:06:13.360
which one defendant is

00:06:13.627 --> 00:06:14.595
available, identifiable, and

00:06:14.862 --> 00:06:17.464
whether or not he can work at

00:06:17.731 --> 00:06:18.499
the chain of command to reach

00:06:18.766 --> 00:06:19.433
more senior figures who may

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.434
have been the architect of

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:21.201
violence.

00:06:21.368 --> 00:06:22.469
They should also expect

00:06:22.736 --> 00:06:24.438
international community to

00:06:24.705 --> 00:06:25.272
support the international

00:06:25.406 --> 00:06:26.340
criminal court, which is

00:06:26.607 --> 00:06:27.274
exercising jurisdiction.

00:06:27.341 --> 00:06:29.576
The court has essentially

00:06:29.843 --> 00:06:31.645
global jurisdiction, a number

00:06:31.912 --> 00:06:33.480
of open investigations in other

00:06:33.747 --> 00:06:34.548
wartime contrast of the

00:06:34.815 --> 00:06:36.450
situations, and so it needs the

00:06:36.717 --> 00:06:37.751
assistance of the international

00:06:38.018 --> 00:06:38.485
community.

00:06:38.485 --> 00:06:41.488
A number of states have now

00:06:41.755 --> 00:06:43.524
personnel, provide additional

00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:44.491
voluntary contributions, et

00:06:44.758 --> 00:06:45.726
cetera, to all of the justice

00:06:45.993 --> 00:06:46.493
efforts.

00:06:46.493 --> 00:06:48.429
And so this is, as you

00:06:48.695 --> 00:06:49.296
mentioned, a daunting task.

00:06:50.431 --> 00:06:50.931
It's an intergenerational

00:06:51.298 --> 00:06:53.434
challenge.
But there are no statutes of

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:54.635
limitations or war crimes and

00:06:54.902 --> 00:06:56.470
other atrocities, and that we

00:06:56.737 --> 00:06:57.738
can be bringing cases for the

00:06:58.005 --> 00:06:58.505
next decade.

00:06:58.539 --> 00:06:59.740
There are still some cases

00:07:00.007 --> 00:07:01.642
being brought against living

00:07:01.909 --> 00:07:02.643
not, sees one of the last cases

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:03.777
that Germany brought was

00:07:04.044 --> 00:07:05.412
against a very other the

00:07:05.679 --> 00:07:07.581
secretary who had been part of

00:07:07.848 --> 00:07:09.583
the holocaust and so we will be

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:10.617
prosecuting these cases for

00:07:10.884 --> 00:07:11.718
many many years to come.

00:07:11.985 --> 00:07:12.920
&gt;&gt; What's important put it in

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:14.521
that kind of historical and

00:07:14.788 --> 00:07:15.689
time line context.

00:07:16.457 --> 00:07:19.593
But I want to ask you about,

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:21.728
the United States is obviously,

00:07:21.995 --> 00:07:22.663
and through your officers,

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.431
prominent in the attempt to get

00:07:24.698 --> 00:07:26.533
a justice, but you are not

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:27.601
members of the icc.

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:29.603
What are the limits of what the

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:30.904
U.S. Can actually do?

00:07:31.338 --> 00:07:35.342
&gt;&gt; I did, we have not ratified

00:07:35.509 --> 00:07:37.344
the treaty, the international

00:07:37.511 --> 00:07:38.278
criminal court, but over the

00:07:38.545 --> 00:07:40.080
years they have been many ways

00:07:40.347 --> 00:07:41.348
that we've been able to support

00:07:41.615 --> 00:07:42.182
the work of the court.

00:07:42.449 --> 00:07:43.350
This includes information

00:07:43.617 --> 00:07:44.985
sharing with the prosecutor,

00:07:45.352 --> 00:07:46.220
includes issues of witness

00:07:46.487 --> 00:07:49.356
protection, and we have helped

00:07:49.356 --> 00:07:51.358
to deliver two suspects to the

00:07:51.425 --> 00:07:51.925
Hague.

00:07:51.959 --> 00:07:52.960
One who showed up at our

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.995
embassy in Kigali, Rwanda,

00:07:55.362 --> 00:07:57.364
asking to be brought The Hague,

00:07:57.364 --> 00:07:58.198
and who was found essentially

00:07:58.465 --> 00:07:59.366
fleeing and central Africa.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.735
Both of those defendants have

00:08:02.002 --> 00:08:02.502
now gone before the court.

00:08:03.637 --> 00:08:07.374
&gt;&gt; That's okay.

00:08:07.441 --> 00:08:08.909
They've gone before the court,

00:08:09.376 --> 00:08:11.011
I guess the big question for

00:08:11.378 --> 00:08:13.380
many Ukrainians and many people

00:08:13.413 --> 00:08:18.919
watching is, will Putin ever be

00:08:19.386 --> 00:08:19.953
charged.

00:08:19.953 --> 00:08:22.122
Have you ever been able to

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:23.957
establish a change a command

00:08:24.224 --> 00:08:24.958
responsibility, and if he is,

00:08:25.392 --> 00:08:26.126
either publicly or sequel

00:08:26.393 --> 00:08:27.961
indicted, will he ever, is

00:08:28.228 --> 00:08:30.063
there a very realistic chance

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.865
but he might be brought before

00:08:32.132 --> 00:08:32.533
a court?

00:08:32.533 --> 00:08:34.935
I go back to Milosevic, lots of

00:08:35.402 --> 00:08:38.005
mission bosnia, who we followed

00:08:38.272 --> 00:08:39.406
the war crimes court against

00:08:39.406 --> 00:08:42.209
him at The Hague, and yeah, he

00:08:42.743 --> 00:08:44.945
was taken, but he was arrested

00:08:45.412 --> 00:08:46.280
inside by his own people.

00:08:47.948 --> 00:08:48.448
And then handed over.

00:08:50.851 --> 00:08:51.418
What do you think in our show

00:08:52.019 --> 00:08:52.386
today?

00:08:52.386 --> 00:08:53.987
&gt;&gt; I don't think slobodan

00:08:54.254 --> 00:08:55.422
Milosevic ever thought he would

00:08:55.422 --> 00:08:56.223
see this type of courtroom.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.424
He was obviously proven wrong.

00:08:57.925 --> 00:08:59.026
This will take time, and there

00:08:59.426 --> 00:09:00.861
may be a political

00:09:01.428 --> 00:09:02.896
transformation within Russia,

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.131
such that he is no longer in

00:09:04.398 --> 00:09:04.898
power.

00:09:04.998 --> 00:09:07.434
This may involve finding

00:09:07.467 --> 00:09:09.436
jurisdiction over lower level

00:09:09.436 --> 00:09:10.037
individuals first.

